Generic single-database configuration.

Project-specific notes (see SCOPE.md §11.2, resolved 2026-08-08):

- No ORM. Migrations are hand-written SQL via `op.execute("...")`, not
  autogenerated from model classes — `env.py`'s `target_metadata` is
  intentionally `None`, so `alembic revision --autogenerate` won't find
  anything to diff against. Use plain `alembic revision -m "..."` and
  write the `upgrade()`/`downgrade()` SQL by hand.
- SQLite has limited `ALTER TABLE` support (no `DROP COLUMN`/constraint
  changes on older SQLite versions). When a migration needs that, use
  `op.batch_alter_table("table_name")` — it rebuilds the table under
  the hood, standard Alembic pattern for SQLite. Not needed for
  simple `CREATE TABLE`/`ADD COLUMN` migrations.
